.TH QFW-SITE-SERVICES 8 "October 2026" "QFw Slurm Cluster" "Administration"
.SH NAME
qfw-site-services \- manage the virtual cluster QFw service plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-site-services
.RB [ \-\-dry-run ]
.RB [ \-\-target " " target ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.BR start | status | stop | restart | recover
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-site-services
starts and stops the administrator-owned site directory, NWQSim DVM and QPM,
IQM QPM, IQM shim QPM, IBM shim QPM, AWS QPM, fake IQM QPM, and QFw Slurm
gateway used by the virtual cluster.
The command runs on
.B slurmctld
as root and invokes the installed QFw service managers on their assigned
service nodes.
.PP
With
.B QFW_DEFW_VERSION=2
the command manages the DEFw v2 prototype's service plane instead.  It runs
beside the v1 plane, with a site configuration, ports, and a run root of its
own, and has only the directory service, the NWQSim QPM, and the fake IQM QPM.
Its
.B all
target is those three, and the other targets are rejected.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B start
Start the selected target.  The default
.B all
target starts the directory service, NWQSim service, IQM service, shim service,
IBM shim service, AWS service, fake IQM service, and gateway in dependency
order.  Partial aggregate startup failure removes only components created by
that invocation.
A target that is not ready is stopped to clean retained runtime state before it
is started.  A ready target is left running.  Starting a QPM or gateway target
requires a ready directory service.
.TP
.B status
Check the selected service managers and gateway endpoint, then print a concise
overall health summary.  An unavailable service is reported as
.BR DOWN ;
that health result does not make the status command fail.  The command fails
only when it cannot complete or interpret a health check.  Machine-readable
status retains the underlying manager record, including stale-state details,
for diagnosis.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the selected target.  The default aggregate action stops the gateway,
fake IQM QPM, AWS QPM, IBM shim QPM, IQM shim QPM, IQM QPM, NWQSim QPM and DVM,
then the directory service.  A targeted directory stop is rejected while the
gateway or a managed QPM remains ready.
.TP
.B restart
Stop and then start the selected target.  A stop failure prevents startup.
.TP
.B recover
Attempt to stop the selected target, tolerate stale or already-stopped state,
and then start it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-target " target"
Select
.BR all ,
.BR directory ,
.BR nwqsim ,
.BR iqm ,
.BR shim ,
.BR ibm ,
.BR aws ,
.BR fake-iqm ,
or
.BR gateway .
The default is
.BR all .
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print the remote commands and dependency order without executing them.
.TP
.B \-\-json
For the
.B status
action, emit one machine-readable status document containing the overall
health, per-service health, and detailed manager records.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The command accepts administrator overrides through
.BR QFW_INSTALL_PREFIX ,
.BR QFW_VENV ,
.BR QFW_SHARED_ROOT ,
.BR QFW_SITE_CONFIG ,
.BR QFW_SITE_RUN_ROOT ,
.BR QFW_DIR_NODE ,
.BR QFW_NWQSIM_NODE ,
.BR QFW_IQM_NODE ,
.BR QFW_SHIM_NODE ,
.BR QFW_IBM_NODE ,
.BR QFW_AWS_NODE ,
.BR QFW_FAKE_IQM_NODE ,
.BR QFW_SIMULATOR_NODES ,
.BR QFW_GATEWAY_HOST ,
.BR QFW_GATEWAY_PORT ,
.BR QFW_GATEWAY_CONFIG ,
.BR QFW_GATEWAY_USER ,
.BR QFW_GATEWAY_LOG_DIR ,
and
.BR QFW_SITE_START_TIMEOUT .
.TP
.B QFW_DEFW_VERSION
Unset or
.B 1
for the v1 service plane,
.B 2
for the DEFw v2 prototype's plane.  It changes the defaults of
.B QFW_SITE_CONFIG
and
.BR QFW_SITE_RUN_ROOT ,
and is forwarded to every service host, where it selects the DEFw the
service managers start.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/openqse/qfw/site.yaml
Default QFw site configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/openqse/qfw/site-defw2.yaml
Default QFw site configuration for the DEFw v2 plane.
.TP
.I /etc/openqse/qfw-slurm/gateway.yaml
Default QFw Slurm gateway configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/qfw-site-services
Default administrator-owned manager state root on each service host.
.TP
.I /var/lib/qfw-site-services-defw2
Default manager state root of the DEFw v2 plane.
.TP
.I /var/lib/qfw-site-services/gateway/supervisor.pid
Default gateway-supervisor PID record.
.TP
.I /var/log/qfw-slurm-gateway/gateway.log
Default gateway-supervisor and process log.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
qfw-site-services start
qfw-site-services status --target nwqsim
qfw-site-services restart --target gateway
qfw-site-services recover --target shim
qfw-site-services recover --target ibm
qfw-site-services recover --target aws
qfw-site-services stop --target all
QFW_DEFW_VERSION=2 qfw-site-services start
.fi
.SH SECURITY
The command requires root for live actions.  It passes protected configuration
paths to the QPM and does not display or replace credential contents.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1),
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1),
.BR qfw-sinfo (1),
.BR qfw-squeue (1)
